1
00:00:02,458 --> 00:00:04,916
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:04,916 --> 00:00:07,500
[wind blasting]

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,625
[all crying out]

4
00:00:12,416 --> 00:00:13,416
[shouting] Whoa!

5
00:00:13,416 --> 00:00:14,875
[grunting with effort]

6
00:00:14,875 --> 00:00:17,125
[shouting]

7
00:00:17,125 --> 00:00:18,333
[grunting with effort]

8
00:00:20,916 --> 00:00:24,625
These unnatural winds
defy all logic!

9
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:27,333
[all shouting] Whoa!

10
00:00:30,666 --> 00:00:33,291
[grunting and grumbling]

11
00:00:33,291 --> 00:00:35,125
[shrieking roar]

12
00:00:40,083 --> 00:00:42,958
I can't leave you all alone
for a minute!

13
00:00:42,958 --> 00:00:44,083
[happy grunting]

14
00:00:44,083 --> 00:00:46,375
[♪♪♪]

15
00:00:48,583 --> 00:00:50,333
[grunting with impact]

16
00:00:51,583 --> 00:00:53,250
Whoa!

17
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:54,250
[grunting with impact]

18
00:00:56,041 --> 00:00:57,333
Wyldfyre!

19
00:00:57,333 --> 00:00:59,416
I have never been more excited
to see you.

20
00:00:59,416 --> 00:01:00,333
Arin?

21
00:01:00,333 --> 00:01:01,250
Why are you here?

22
00:01:01,250 --> 00:01:03,458
I thought you peaced out.

23
00:01:03,458 --> 00:01:05,791
[Arin] I'm trying
not to let the world end.

24
00:01:05,791 --> 00:01:09,083
Well, I'm here now,
so it won't.

25
00:01:09,083 --> 00:01:10,666
[grunting with effort]

26
00:01:10,666 --> 00:01:12,250
Oof!

27
00:01:13,833 --> 00:01:15,916
[♪♪♪]

28
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:18,291
[revving]

29
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,375
[Riyu shrieking]

30
00:01:34,041 --> 00:01:35,083
[grunting with impact]

31
00:01:39,875 --> 00:01:41,416
Riyu!

32
00:01:50,875 --> 00:01:51,750
[groaning softly]

33
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:55,291
[grunting with effort]

34
00:01:57,833 --> 00:01:59,208
You okay, boy?

35
00:01:59,208 --> 00:02:01,333
[grumbling softly]

36
00:02:01,333 --> 00:02:02,541
[wheezing]

37
00:02:06,583 --> 00:02:08,625
That thing is way cool!

38
00:02:08,625 --> 00:02:09,625
Can I try?

39
00:02:09,625 --> 00:02:11,375
It won't look as cool on you.

40
00:02:11,375 --> 00:02:12,500
Hurtful.

41
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:14,916
We have more pressing problems,
you two.

42
00:02:14,916 --> 00:02:16,958
Anyone see
where the Forbidden Five went?

43
00:02:18,583 --> 00:02:19,625
I...

44
00:02:19,625 --> 00:02:21,875
I had the last two blades.

45
00:02:21,875 --> 00:02:24,000
I know I should have just
flown off with them,

46
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,750
but I tried to save Ras,

47
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:28,625
then Rox attacked me.

48
00:02:30,291 --> 00:02:31,458
Hold on.

49
00:02:31,458 --> 00:02:33,666
If the Five have
all the blades,

50
00:02:33,666 --> 00:02:35,500
doesn't that mean
they can free--

51
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,791
[deep rumbling,
all yelping in alarm]

52
00:02:41,083 --> 00:02:42,916
-[heavy slamming]
-[gasping in shock]

53
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,583
[together] Thunderfang!

54
00:02:49,791 --> 00:02:51,958
[snarling]

55
00:02:51,958 --> 00:02:53,916
[deafening roar]

56
00:02:53,916 --> 00:02:57,125
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

57
00:02:57,125 --> 00:03:00,125
♪ Together we will rise ♪

58
00:03:00,125 --> 00:03:03,083
♪ We fight ♪

59
00:03:03,083 --> 00:03:06,666
♪ Be a ninja for what's right ♪

60
00:03:07,958 --> 00:03:08,958
[thunderclap]

61
00:03:08,958 --> 00:03:10,250
[deafening roar]

62
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:17,416
I knew he was big.

63
00:03:17,416 --> 00:03:20,000
Yeah, but that is like big-big.

64
00:03:23,666 --> 00:03:26,875
[wind gusting]

65
00:03:33,083 --> 00:03:34,916
Be safe, Ninja.

66
00:03:39,083 --> 00:03:40,458
Cole...

67
00:03:40,458 --> 00:03:42,000
I think the MergeQuakes
are back.

68
00:03:43,583 --> 00:03:47,250
No, this is
something different.

69
00:03:47,250 --> 00:03:49,958
We better
gather up the Finders.

70
00:03:55,583 --> 00:03:56,708
My documents!

71
00:03:56,708 --> 00:03:58,750
This weather is unauthorized!

72
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:03,125
[Thunderfang] Source Dragons!

73
00:04:03,125 --> 00:04:07,666
You will rue the day
you rejected me!

74
00:04:07,666 --> 00:04:09,875
Where'd the Forbidden Five go?

75
00:04:09,875 --> 00:04:11,416
Maybe Thunderfang ate 'em.

76
00:04:11,416 --> 00:04:13,875
Would explain why
he's in such a foul mood.

77
00:04:13,875 --> 00:04:15,833
You know, 'cause they're
probably hard to digest?

78
00:04:15,833 --> 00:04:16,833
Make you sick, and--

79
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:17,791
I got it.

80
00:04:17,791 --> 00:04:18,875
You didn't laugh.

81
00:04:18,875 --> 00:04:20,541
I reacted correctly.

82
00:04:20,541 --> 00:04:21,833
[deafening roar]

83
00:04:21,833 --> 00:04:24,458
I have no idea
how we beat this thing,

84
00:04:24,458 --> 00:04:26,708
except there's one of him
and ten of us,

85
00:04:26,708 --> 00:04:28,833
so let's come at him
from all sides!

86
00:04:28,833 --> 00:04:30,375
[Wyldfyre] Works for me!

87
00:04:30,375 --> 00:04:32,583
Ninja... go!

88
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,750
[♪♪♪]

89
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:44,208
[roaring]

90
00:04:45,458 --> 00:04:47,041
[gasping and screaming]

91
00:04:47,041 --> 00:04:49,875
[grunting with impact]

92
00:04:49,875 --> 00:04:53,041
[Thunderfang] Last time,
it took an Arc Dragon of Focus

93
00:04:53,041 --> 00:04:54,416
to defeat me!

94
00:04:54,416 --> 00:04:58,750
You puny mortals have no chance!

95
00:04:58,750 --> 00:05:00,166
[yelping]

96
00:05:00,166 --> 00:05:01,250
[grunting with impact]

97
00:05:06,166 --> 00:05:07,916
Much appreciated.

98
00:05:09,625 --> 00:05:10,583
Ooh!

99
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:12,625
H'yah!

100
00:05:12,625 --> 00:05:13,791
[earthquake rumbling]

101
00:05:13,791 --> 00:05:15,083
Ah!

102
00:05:21,166 --> 00:05:25,333
You ugly jerks are an insult
to dragons everywhere!

103
00:05:25,333 --> 00:05:26,750
[engine revving]

104
00:05:27,750 --> 00:05:29,541
[grunting with effort]

105
00:05:31,041 --> 00:05:33,250
[snarling]

106
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,083
[gasping in fright]

107
00:05:34,083 --> 00:05:35,041
H'ah!

108
00:05:36,208 --> 00:05:37,166
[grumbling]

109
00:05:38,208 --> 00:05:39,625
Like that? Have some more!

110
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,083
[roaring]

111
00:05:42,083 --> 00:05:44,291
[yelping and groaning]

112
00:05:47,416 --> 00:05:48,916
[gasping]

113
00:05:50,083 --> 00:05:51,416
[stomping]

114
00:05:51,416 --> 00:05:52,541
[Frak] Thanks, man.

115
00:05:52,541 --> 00:05:53,541
[Arin]
Couldn't let you get hurt

116
00:05:53,541 --> 00:05:55,416
on our first
Ninja adventure together!

117
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:57,708
[gasping]

118
00:05:58,708 --> 00:06:00,291
[roaring]

119
00:06:00,291 --> 00:06:01,791
There you are.

120
00:06:03,750 --> 00:06:05,750
Ras! Look out!

121
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:07,041
[grunting with effort]

122
00:06:11,875 --> 00:06:13,041
H'yah!

123
00:06:13,916 --> 00:06:15,500
[Arin] Leave him alone!

124
00:06:16,708 --> 00:06:18,375
Aah!

125
00:06:18,375 --> 00:06:21,083
[grunting in pain]

126
00:06:22,666 --> 00:06:24,083
[snarling]

127
00:06:24,083 --> 00:06:25,583
[gasping in fright]

128
00:06:28,916 --> 00:06:29,958
[grunting with effort]

129
00:06:35,541 --> 00:06:37,458
[roaring]

130
00:06:38,583 --> 00:06:40,166
[Riyu screeching]

131
00:06:40,166 --> 00:06:41,708
[circuits shorting]

132
00:06:43,166 --> 00:06:45,625
[Wyldfyre] Can't you
do anything without my help?

133
00:06:46,791 --> 00:06:48,250
Hi'yah!

134
00:06:49,208 --> 00:06:50,708
-[Thunderfang roaring]
-Whoo!

135
00:06:50,708 --> 00:06:52,708
That was satisfying.

136
00:06:53,833 --> 00:06:55,208
[circuits shorting]

137
00:06:55,208 --> 00:06:56,916
Whoa!

138
00:07:01,083 --> 00:07:02,041
[gasping]

139
00:07:03,750 --> 00:07:07,166
[♪♪♪]

140
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:14,500
[Thunderfang gasping]

141
00:07:18,416 --> 00:07:19,500
[deafening roar]

142
00:07:19,500 --> 00:07:21,000
[wind gusting]

143
00:07:22,333 --> 00:07:26,708
[Thunderfang] I smell the power
of a Source Dragon Conduit!

144
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:34,958
A direct line to
the Source Dragons themselves?

145
00:07:34,958 --> 00:07:37,375
-You!
-[Lloyd gasping]

146
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:45,416
Draining a Conduit's power
will be transcendent!

147
00:07:56,833 --> 00:07:59,416
Whose energy do you channel?

148
00:07:59,416 --> 00:08:00,541
Motion?

149
00:08:00,541 --> 00:08:03,125
That incessant busybody?

150
00:08:03,125 --> 00:08:06,083
Or the self-obsessed Strength?

151
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:10,000
[slamming dirt, claw dragging]

152
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,250
[Lloyd grunting with effort]

153
00:08:11,250 --> 00:08:13,041
[Thunderfang] Or is it Life?

154
00:08:13,041 --> 00:08:14,041
[roaring]

155
00:08:14,041 --> 00:08:15,625
[Lloyd gasping wearily]

156
00:08:18,416 --> 00:08:22,500
[Thunderfang]
How ironic would that be?

157
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:24,708
[Lloyd yelping]

158
00:08:24,708 --> 00:08:26,500
[groaning with impact]

159
00:08:29,916 --> 00:08:32,458
[inhaling]

160
00:08:36,875 --> 00:08:37,833
[Thunderfang yelps in pain]

161
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,250
[squawking]

162
00:08:50,333 --> 00:08:54,041
You need to shelter
from this natural disaster, sir.

163
00:08:54,041 --> 00:08:56,333
There's nothing natural
about this.

164
00:08:58,833 --> 00:09:00,708
[wind gusting]

165
00:09:00,708 --> 00:09:02,083
[squawking]

166
00:09:04,625 --> 00:09:06,416
I've got you, Fritz!

167
00:09:16,291 --> 00:09:17,250
H'yah!

168
00:09:17,250 --> 00:09:19,875
[grunting with effort]

169
00:09:21,166 --> 00:09:23,250
On your feet
if you want to survive!

170
00:09:25,875 --> 00:09:27,541
[grunting with effort]

171
00:09:27,541 --> 00:09:28,666
Huah!

172
00:09:28,666 --> 00:09:31,208
[Nya] Not bad
for some rando mercenary.

173
00:09:36,708 --> 00:09:38,625
Aren't you supposed
to be unstoppable?

174
00:09:38,625 --> 00:09:40,041
[roaring]

175
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:42,375
Aah!

176
00:09:42,375 --> 00:09:45,166
I knew I should never fly
not on a dragon!

177
00:09:46,125 --> 00:09:47,750
-Aah!
-Wyldfyre!

178
00:09:48,875 --> 00:09:50,333
[yelping]

179
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:52,250
[grunting with impact]

180
00:09:52,250 --> 00:09:53,583
-[groaning]
-You hurt?

181
00:09:53,583 --> 00:09:56,083
No way, I don't get hurt.

182
00:09:56,083 --> 00:09:57,125
[wincing groan]

183
00:09:57,125 --> 00:09:59,458
Hey, I gave it some thought.

184
00:09:59,458 --> 00:10:01,875
You would look really cool
in that mech.

185
00:10:01,875 --> 00:10:03,625
Seriously?
You're thinking about that now?

186
00:10:03,625 --> 00:10:04,625
Really cool!

187
00:10:06,375 --> 00:10:07,333
You're right,

188
00:10:07,333 --> 00:10:08,875
this is pretty cool.

189
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:11,666
H'yah!

190
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:18,250
[grunting with effort]

191
00:10:20,708 --> 00:10:22,458
[stone crumbling]

192
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,750
[♪♪♪]

193
00:10:29,083 --> 00:10:30,208
Couldn't let you get hurt

194
00:10:30,208 --> 00:10:32,458
on our first
Ninja adventure together.

195
00:10:34,375 --> 00:10:36,958
High velocity contact
at the anterior

196
00:10:36,958 --> 00:10:38,541
may yield results.

197
00:10:38,541 --> 00:10:39,541
Acknowledged!

198
00:10:44,166 --> 00:10:45,208
[roaring]

199
00:10:53,208 --> 00:10:54,833
[Thunderfang] Pests!

200
00:10:54,833 --> 00:10:56,541
[grunting with impact]

201
00:10:56,541 --> 00:10:58,041
[engine revving]

202
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,458
[foot stomping]

203
00:11:02,458 --> 00:11:04,666
[grunting with impact]

204
00:11:04,666 --> 00:11:07,000
[roaring]

205
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,875
[Thunderfang] Conduit!

206
00:11:10,875 --> 00:11:12,208
[snarling]

207
00:11:16,333 --> 00:11:17,791
Oh, come on!

208
00:11:17,791 --> 00:11:19,125
This is a loaner!

209
00:11:19,125 --> 00:11:21,375
Now you just
scratched it all up!

210
00:11:22,833 --> 00:11:24,250
[yelping]

211
00:11:25,250 --> 00:11:26,333
[grunting with impact]

212
00:11:27,458 --> 00:11:29,083
[grunting with effort]

213
00:11:31,375 --> 00:11:32,750
Ah!

214
00:11:35,875 --> 00:11:38,250
[energy crackling]

215
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:41,791
No way...

216
00:11:41,791 --> 00:11:43,875
[♪♪♪]

217
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:50,291
Thought I'd...
lightning up the mood!

218
00:11:50,291 --> 00:11:52,125
<i>And </i>terrible puns?

219
00:11:56,791 --> 00:11:58,083
[worried grunting]

220
00:11:59,208 --> 00:12:00,458
[shrieking]

221
00:12:01,208 --> 00:12:03,500
[stomping footsteps]

222
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,625
[Thunderfang] Conduit!

223
00:12:05,625 --> 00:12:06,750
[Lloyd screaming]

224
00:12:08,083 --> 00:12:09,208
[gasping in horror]

225
00:12:10,916 --> 00:12:12,916
Lloyd! Lloyd!

226
00:12:13,750 --> 00:12:14,625
[gasping]

227
00:12:14,625 --> 00:12:15,541
Unh!

228
00:12:21,166 --> 00:12:23,625
[screaming] No!

229
00:12:26,458 --> 00:12:28,500
[evil cackling]

230
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:30,958
[Arin yelping]

231
00:12:32,541 --> 00:12:34,375
[screaming]

232
00:12:42,041 --> 00:12:44,750
[powerful roaring]

233
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:45,708
No!

234
00:12:47,166 --> 00:12:48,333
[grunting with effort]

235
00:12:48,333 --> 00:12:49,916
[♪♪♪]

236
00:12:49,916 --> 00:12:53,208
Lloyd! Lloyd! Come on!

237
00:12:53,208 --> 00:12:55,000
No!

238
00:12:58,250 --> 00:13:01,000
[roaring]

239
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,750
[screaming]

240
00:13:02,750 --> 00:13:04,916
[Thunderfang] Source Dragons!

241
00:13:04,916 --> 00:13:06,875
I have reaped the soul

242
00:13:06,875 --> 00:13:09,708
of one of your mortal Conduits!

243
00:13:09,708 --> 00:13:12,958
You can deny me no longer!

244
00:13:12,958 --> 00:13:15,916
I know you hear me,

245
00:13:15,916 --> 00:13:18,000
and I will not stop

246
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:22,708
until I devour
all of your souls as well!

247
00:13:22,708 --> 00:13:24,166
Souls?

248
00:13:29,791 --> 00:13:30,916
[gasping]

249
00:13:31,875 --> 00:13:33,208
<i>[Arin] What is this stuff?</i>

250
00:13:33,208 --> 00:13:34,375
<i>[departed soul] Don't ask me.</i>

251
00:13:34,375 --> 00:13:37,083
<i>Drinking it is what helps souls</i>
<i>move on.</i>

252
00:13:38,666 --> 00:13:41,666
"Helps souls move on..."

253
00:13:47,125 --> 00:13:50,416
[grunting with effort]

254
00:13:52,375 --> 00:13:54,333
[gasping]

255
00:13:59,375 --> 00:14:01,083
[Ras] Don't be a fool.

256
00:14:01,083 --> 00:14:03,791
A moving target
through the winds of chaos?

257
00:14:03,791 --> 00:14:06,541
You don't have enough anger
for that kind of strength.

258
00:14:08,708 --> 00:14:10,166
<i>The Arin I know,</i>

259
00:14:10,166 --> 00:14:12,083
<i>my best friend,</i>

260
00:14:12,083 --> 00:14:14,500
<i>his strength comes</i>
<i>from his kindness,</i>

261
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:16,333
<i>his generosity,</i>

262
00:14:16,333 --> 00:14:17,666
<i>his hope.</i>

263
00:14:18,791 --> 00:14:19,958
[Arin] You're right.

264
00:14:19,958 --> 00:14:22,750
I don't have enough anger
to pull this off...

265
00:14:22,750 --> 00:14:25,958
[♪♪♪]

266
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:36,000
I have something better.

267
00:14:37,875 --> 00:14:41,041
Ninja...

268
00:14:41,041 --> 00:14:42,041
Go!

269
00:14:42,041 --> 00:14:43,041
[♪♪♪]

270
00:14:49,250 --> 00:14:50,416
[Thunderfang] What?!

271
00:14:50,416 --> 00:14:51,458
[snarling]

272
00:14:51,458 --> 00:14:52,583
[♪♪♪]

273
00:14:54,375 --> 00:14:55,750
[grunting with effort]

274
00:14:55,750 --> 00:14:57,791
[Riyu groaning]

275
00:14:57,791 --> 00:14:59,708
This is weird, right?

276
00:14:59,708 --> 00:15:01,791
Arin threw something at him.

277
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:05,375
[grunting]

278
00:15:05,375 --> 00:15:06,541
[roaring]

279
00:15:07,875 --> 00:15:11,791
[Thunderfang] Impossible...

280
00:15:11,791 --> 00:15:13,791
[crumbling]

281
00:15:20,541 --> 00:15:23,458
[♪♪♪]

282
00:15:32,416 --> 00:15:33,875
[bursting]

283
00:15:40,125 --> 00:15:41,208
[crying out]

284
00:15:56,416 --> 00:15:57,583
[gasping]

285
00:15:57,583 --> 00:15:59,416
[breathing hard]

286
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:01,208
Lloyd!

287
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:04,250
[gasping]

288
00:16:05,416 --> 00:16:07,333
[storm dissipating]

289
00:16:08,333 --> 00:16:10,375
I've had
some really weird days,

290
00:16:10,375 --> 00:16:13,666
but this might be
the weirdest one yet.

291
00:16:13,666 --> 00:16:15,291
[all laughing]

292
00:16:15,291 --> 00:16:16,333
Oh...

293
00:16:20,833 --> 00:16:22,583
[Riyu grunting happily]

294
00:16:22,583 --> 00:16:24,083
[grumbling]

295
00:16:25,416 --> 00:16:27,458
[♪♪♪]

296
00:16:31,791 --> 00:16:33,916
Thank you, Wyldfyre,

297
00:16:33,916 --> 00:16:35,083
and I'm sure

298
00:16:35,083 --> 00:16:36,875
some of the other Ninja helped.

299
00:16:37,833 --> 00:16:40,958
We are so sorry
for our actions.

300
00:16:42,250 --> 00:16:44,791
We know
you weren't yourselves, Tyr.

301
00:16:44,791 --> 00:16:47,666
We owe you Ninja our freedom.

302
00:16:47,666 --> 00:16:50,125
It was really Arin
who freed you.

303
00:16:52,125 --> 00:16:54,291
[Tyr] Then you are
a great hero, Arin.

304
00:16:54,291 --> 00:16:55,291
Oh!

305
00:16:55,291 --> 00:16:56,958
Well, not really.

306
00:16:56,958 --> 00:16:59,541
I was the reason
the Five freed Thunderfang

307
00:16:59,541 --> 00:17:00,750
to begin with,

308
00:17:00,750 --> 00:17:03,416
and fighting him
was a group effort, and he--

309
00:17:03,416 --> 00:17:04,875
--Is a great hero.

310
00:17:04,875 --> 00:17:05,875
[Ras] Arin...

311
00:17:07,291 --> 00:17:08,916
Time to go.

312
00:17:10,708 --> 00:17:12,750
[Riyu growling]

313
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,500
I'm sorry, everyone.

314
00:17:16,500 --> 00:17:18,166
My parents...

315
00:17:18,166 --> 00:17:20,041
[Kai] What?

316
00:17:20,041 --> 00:17:21,125
No...

317
00:17:21,125 --> 00:17:24,000
Arin, you know better.

318
00:17:25,500 --> 00:17:27,125
Lloyd?

319
00:17:28,125 --> 00:17:29,125
I'm sorry too.

320
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,750
What the heck
is going on here?

321
00:17:31,750 --> 00:17:33,208
Arin, wait!

322
00:17:34,583 --> 00:17:36,333
You're coming with us?

323
00:17:36,333 --> 00:17:38,250
Together forever, right?

324
00:17:39,708 --> 00:17:42,958
And why should I allow you
to travel in my company?

325
00:17:42,958 --> 00:17:44,250
You don't think

326
00:17:44,250 --> 00:17:46,625
having the Elemental Master
of Technology

327
00:17:46,625 --> 00:17:48,500
will help us on our mission?

328
00:17:49,583 --> 00:17:51,291
[grumbling]

329
00:17:52,291 --> 00:17:53,958
You don't have to do this.

330
00:17:53,958 --> 00:17:55,000
Of course I do.

331
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,875
Who else is gonna
watch out for you?

332
00:18:00,166 --> 00:18:02,625
Are you seriously going to
let Ras leave with them?

333
00:18:02,625 --> 00:18:04,750
They're free to make
their own decisions.

334
00:18:04,750 --> 00:18:07,250
That's the difference
between us and Ras.

335
00:18:07,250 --> 00:18:09,958
And you're not worried
about them?

336
00:18:09,958 --> 00:18:12,125
I didn't say that.

337
00:18:13,291 --> 00:18:15,583
[groaning sadly]

338
00:18:16,375 --> 00:18:17,250
There!

339
00:18:20,375 --> 00:18:21,958
[grunting with effort]

340
00:18:23,833 --> 00:18:24,833
[groaning]

341
00:18:24,833 --> 00:18:25,833
Ah!

342
00:18:25,833 --> 00:18:27,166
You need a splint on that leg.

343
00:18:27,166 --> 00:18:29,500
Let's get you
back to the Monastery.

344
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:31,250
Why are you gonna help me?

345
00:18:31,250 --> 00:18:34,125
I know who you are,
you big dummy.

346
00:18:34,125 --> 00:18:37,250
Uh, yeah,
a secret man of mystery

347
00:18:37,250 --> 00:18:38,291
whose identity will never--

348
00:18:38,291 --> 00:18:40,416
Elemental Lightning?
Really?

349
00:18:40,416 --> 00:18:41,666
So?

350
00:18:41,666 --> 00:18:44,083
Lots of people probably have
Elemental Lightning.

351
00:18:44,083 --> 00:18:45,083
-Nope.
-[groaning]

352
00:18:47,708 --> 00:18:48,958
[together] Jay?

353
00:18:48,958 --> 00:18:50,041
Don't pretend you know me!

354
00:18:50,041 --> 00:18:53,083
And I'm not going
to your stupid Monastery!

355
00:18:53,083 --> 00:18:56,625
Normal people don't just
have monasteries!

356
00:18:56,625 --> 00:18:57,916
It's weird!

357
00:18:57,916 --> 00:18:59,583
And another thing--

358
00:18:59,583 --> 00:19:02,041
Ow! Owie-ow-ow-ow-ow! [sobs]

359
00:19:02,041 --> 00:19:03,791
Get me to your Monastery!

360
00:19:03,791 --> 00:19:05,250
Can't you see I need help?

361
00:19:06,958 --> 00:19:08,541
[♪♪♪]

362
00:19:08,541 --> 00:19:10,833
Congratulations, Ninja!

363
00:19:11,958 --> 00:19:13,291
You did it!

364
00:19:16,166 --> 00:19:17,416
I guess,

365
00:19:17,416 --> 00:19:21,291
but this win doesn't exactly
feel like a win.

366
00:19:21,291 --> 00:19:24,916
Well, our guests
would disagree.

367
00:19:24,916 --> 00:19:28,083
Guests?

368
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:31,416
Lobbo-lobbo crushes
pie-eating record!

369
00:19:31,416 --> 00:19:34,541
[all cheering]

370
00:19:34,541 --> 00:19:35,666
[cheering and celebrating]

371
00:19:35,666 --> 00:19:38,500
[crowd chanting]
Lobbo! Lobbo! Lobbo!

372
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:41,625
[♪♪♪]

373
00:19:43,250 --> 00:19:44,916
Wyldfyre!

374
00:19:44,916 --> 00:19:47,500
I knew you'd save us!

375
00:19:48,750 --> 00:19:49,750
Rawr...

376
00:19:49,750 --> 00:19:52,250
Rawr!
[snarling playfully]

377
00:19:52,250 --> 00:19:54,875
Mr. Frohicky makes great pizza!

378
00:19:54,875 --> 00:19:56,125
Without flies, even!

379
00:19:56,125 --> 00:19:57,916
Whoa. Jay?

380
00:19:57,916 --> 00:19:59,166
[wincing] Ah!

381
00:19:59,166 --> 00:20:00,666
I can't believe it!

382
00:20:00,666 --> 00:20:01,666
Bring it in!

383
00:20:01,666 --> 00:20:03,083
Get away, weirdo.

384
00:20:03,916 --> 00:20:05,791
Still no memory?

385
00:20:05,791 --> 00:20:07,666
I got plenty of memories, bub.

386
00:20:07,666 --> 00:20:10,166
Just none of them are of you.

387
00:20:10,166 --> 00:20:12,125
Wow. Okay...

388
00:20:12,125 --> 00:20:13,958
[groaning]

389
00:20:15,041 --> 00:20:16,875
[laughing and celebrating]

390
00:20:16,875 --> 00:20:18,500
And still no Arin?

391
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:21,000
He and Sora went with Ras.

392
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:22,125
Arin thinks Ras

393
00:20:22,125 --> 00:20:23,833
can bring his parents
back from the dead.

394
00:20:23,833 --> 00:20:24,833
Dead?

395
00:20:24,833 --> 00:20:26,458
[scoffing] I know for a fact

396
00:20:26,458 --> 00:20:28,500
that Arin kid's parents
are alive.

397
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:29,958
What?

398
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,500
Hello? I worked
for the Administration.

399
00:20:32,500 --> 00:20:35,250
Head of the Department
of Realm Reassignment?

400
00:20:35,250 --> 00:20:36,708
What do you think I did there?

401
00:20:36,708 --> 00:20:37,916
I know exactly where

402
00:20:37,916 --> 00:20:39,708
Arin's parents
were reassigned,

403
00:20:39,708 --> 00:20:41,791
and it's really, really weird.

404
00:20:43,291 --> 00:20:45,166
[bucket rattling in the wind]

405
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,500
Dearly Departed,

406
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:56,125
this may come as a shock,

407
00:20:56,125 --> 00:20:59,250
but you have transitioned
out of the living world.

408
00:20:59,250 --> 00:21:02,041
I vow to protect you
as you move into...

409
00:21:04,041 --> 00:21:06,458
Okay, wow.

410
00:21:06,458 --> 00:21:07,500
You're a big one.

411
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:08,500
[distant screeching]

412
00:21:14,291 --> 00:21:15,583
[snarling]

413
00:21:15,583 --> 00:21:16,500
Stay back.

414
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:17,625
I'll ward them off.

415
00:21:17,625 --> 00:21:19,083
[barking and snarling]

416
00:21:19,083 --> 00:21:21,500
[Thunderfang]
I can handle myself.

417
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,541
[snarling]

418
00:21:26,083 --> 00:21:27,541
What?

419
00:21:28,791 --> 00:21:30,791
That's impossible.

420
00:21:30,791 --> 00:21:32,416
[Thunderfang] In the afterlife,

421
00:21:32,416 --> 00:21:35,541
anything is possible.

422
00:21:37,250 --> 00:21:39,750
[screaming]

423
00:21:42,250 --> 00:21:43,791
[evil cackling]

424
00:21:43,791 --> 00:21:48,000
[maniacal laughter]

425
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,750
[♪♪♪]

